{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>For I did not know.</b> This too is his disgrace — and under compulsion he admitted it. He had been boasting that he knows the knowledge of the Most High, yet his own mouth testified: ״I did not know״ (ibid.)." "<b>If it is evil in Your eyes I will turn back for You.</b> This reply is to brazenly challenge the Omnipresent. He said to Him: He Himself commanded me to go, and You, an angel, nullify His words! He is accustomed to this — that He says a thing and an angel retracts it. He said to Abraham ״Take now your son״ etc. (Genesis 22), and through an angel nullified His word. So I too — if it is evil in Your eyes, I must turn back."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:18.140287440Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}